&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will join the Product Management team building Luno’s institutional business: the activation, digital asset account infrastructure and issuance products that let businesses, institutions and partners operate on Luno’s rails. The portfolio spans Luno Institutional and BlockTower, the group’s stablecoin issuance business. You&#39;ll report to the Group Product Manager and work in the BlockTower pod with dedicated engineering and UX partners.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role in a nutshell:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;BlockTower is the group’s institutional stablecoin issuance business, starting with ZARU, the South African rand stablecoin. You&#39;ll own the products institutions touch: the self-service issuance platform, where treasury teams mint, redeem, distribute yield and report, and Wallet as a Service, which lets those institutions use and offer stablecoins inside their own&amp;nbsp; products and flows. Your job is to turn a working product into a repeatable one, and to build the foundation on which future local-currency stablecoins launch in new markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your mission will be:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The issuance platform: the portal, mint and redeem flows, yield distribution, user and access management, approval workflows, statements and reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wallet as a Service: how institutions embed wallets into their own platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The boundary: What the platform needs from the underlying Luno infrastructure, and holding the line on what BlockTower owns itself&lt;/li&gt;
